// F28, the half left open when the parser-level check landed: inside a function body `-- a note`
// is a legal double negation of `a`, so nothing failed until an unrelated "undefined variable",
// and the comment was invisible. A lexical rule scoped to a line's first non-whitespace reaches it
// without touching arithmetic.
fn main() {
    -- count the items
    print(1)
}
